<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    Entitlements the `mia` binary needs to keep a Secure Enclave key in the
    keychain, which is what lets the X.509-SVID credential store survive a
    restart on macOS (see docs/features/F17-x509-svid.md).

    Both entries are *restricted*: they are only honoured on a binary signed by
    a real Apple Developer team. Ad-hoc signing does not work — AMFI kills the
    process at launch. Replace TEAMID with the team identifier of the signing
    certificate, and keep the group in sync with the bundle identifier.

    Without these, `mia` still runs: `credstore::with_sealer` finds it cannot
    persist an Enclave key (errSecMissingEntitlement, -34018) and falls back to
    the fingerprint-derived machine key.
  -->
  <key>com.apple.application-identifier</key>
  <string>TEAMID.com.ferrogate.mia</string>
  <key>keychain-access-groups</key>
  <array>
    <string>TEAMID.com.ferrogate.mia</string>
  </array>
</dict>
</plist>
